      "templateText": "Department of Electrical & Electronic Engineering\nInternational Islamic University Chittagong\nKumira, Sitakunda, Chattogram\n\n10 September 2026\n\nThe Customer Relations Manager\nSiemens Industrial Automation Ltd.\nPlot 32, Gulshan Avenue, Dhaka-1212\n\nSubject: Urgent Complaint Regarding Defective Digital Oscilloscopes (Invoice #SI-8891)\n\nDear Sir,\n\nI am writing to register an urgent formal complaint regarding our consignment of fifteen (15) Digital Storage Oscilloscopes (Model DSO-5000) received on September 3, 2026, under Purchase Order #IIUC/EEE/2026/044.\n\nUpon unboxing and conducting standard calibration tests in our laboratory on September 5, 2026, our technical committee discovered significant defects:\n1. Five (5) units (Serial Numbers: DSO-9941 through DSO-9945) exhibit severe channel crosstalk and failing LCD backlight inverters.\n2. Two (2) power cables and probe sets were missing entirely from the carton boxes.\n3. The packaging showed signs of severe moisture damage incurred during transit.\n\nAs our undergraduate semester laboratory examinations commence on October 1, 2026, this defect poses a critical interruption to our academic schedule. \n\nUnder Clause 7 of our procurement agreement, we request that you dispatch a certified technician to inspect the consignment and replace the five defective units within seven (7) business days. Failing this, we shall be compelled to cancel the contract and seek liquidated damages.\n\nWe anticipate your immediate intervention in this matter.\n\nYours faithfully,\n\n(Signature)\nEngr. Tareq Ahmed\nSenior Laboratory Engineer, Department of EEE\nInternational Islamic University Chittagong",
      "tips": "Maintain a firm yet courteous professional tone. Cite specific serial numbers, invoice numbers, delivery dates, and a firm deadline for remediation."
